## Background worker

```
{% if worker == "taskiq" %}
uv run taskiq worker {{ package_name }}.worker:broker --app-dir src
{% elif worker == "celery" %}
PYTHONPATH=src uv run celery -A {{ package_name }}.worker.celery_app worker --loglevel=info
{% endif %}
```
{% if worker == "taskiq" %}
`--app-dir src` is needed because the app lives under `src/` — without it
the worker can't find `{{ package_name }}`.
{% elif worker == "celery" %}
`PYTHONPATH=src` is needed because the app lives under `src/` — without
it the worker can't find `{{ package_name }}`.
{% endif %}
{% if redis %}
Needs Redis running and reachable at `REDIS_URL` (see `.env`).
{% endif %}

Try it: `POST /tasks/add?a=1&b=2` enqueues a task and returns its id.
{% endif %}
{% if redis %}

## Redis

A ready-to-use async client is exported as `redis_client` from
`src/{{ package_name }}/core/redis.py`. Needs Redis running and reachable
at `REDIS_URL` (see `.env`).
{% endif %}
